275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The Zerodha-like Trading Application is a full-stack web-based platform developed using the MERN stack \(MongoDB, Express.js, React.js, and Node.js\) to simulate a real-world online trading environment. The application is designed to provide users with a responsive, secure, and user-friendly interface for analyzing financial markets, managing investments, and executing trades efficiently. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (It follows a layered architecture where the React-based frontend handles user interaction and visualization, the Node.js and Express backend manages business logic and API communication, and MongoDB stores user data, portfolios, and transaction records. The platform includes key features such as real-time portfolio tracking, advanced charting for technical analysis, fast order execution, profit and loss monitoring, and detailed performance reports. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Additionally, it offers fund management capabilities, price alerts, and integrated tools for enhanced analytics. The user interface is divided into essential modules, including a homepage for onboarding and education, a dashboard for real-time portfolio insights with graphical representations, and a support portal for user assistance and issue resolution. The application also incorporates testing using Jest and React Testing Library to ensure reliability and proper functionality of UI components and trading operations. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Overall, this project demonstrates a realistic and scalable trading system, combining modern web technologies, clean architecture, and practical financial features, making it a strong representation of a professional trading platform suitable for both academic and portfolio purposes.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
